108:`in_space` is not executable by `anon`. Only write paths reach it as the caller, and `anon`'s reads use `my_space_ids`.
110:`anon` holds only `SELECT` on the contributor tables, and its reads fail with a permission error on `ResourceAccess` until public access adds the grants below.
114:`anon` will read public nodes, their files and their authors (ENG-1837). The "Public access" entries above, and `anon`'s `SELECT` on `Space`, the contributor tables and the views, are grants made ahead of that work. `anon` can't execute the functions that write, except `get_secret_token`. Keep them: rule 1 means that removing one fails those queries with a permission error. ENG-1837 also has to grant `anon` `SELECT` on `Concept`, `Content`, `Document`, `FileReference` and `ResourceAccess`, and open `storage_select_assets_access` to `anon`, which today applies only to `authenticated`.
124:- `my_groups` reads `auth.users` (`auth_users_exposed` and `security_definer_view`). Groups are rows in `auth.users`, with the synthetic email `{group name}@groups.discoursegraphs.com` set by the `create-group` edge function. The view returns only the id and name of the groups the current user belongs to; `anon` gets no rows. It must run as its owner, because clients can't read `auth.users`. This stays.
127:- `anon_security_definer_function_executable` for the four functions in the table above.
143:- New table: enable RLS, because `authenticated` can read and write it by default. Write policies for each operation, and grant `anon` only what anonymous readers need. Add visibility scenarios to `features/`, like `features/conceptAccess.feature`.
147:- New function that `anon` reaches, directly, through a policy or through a view: grant it to `anon` in its schema file and in the migration.
149:- New or changed view: keep existing names and columns, and mirror the table's access rules. Revoke `INSERT`, `UPDATE` and `DELETE` from `authenticated`, and grant `SELECT` to `anon` if anonymous readers need it.
162:- ENG-2442: function grants made explicit, and new functions no longer executable by `anon`.
166:- ENG-2466: default privileges set in `base.sql` instead of taken from the Supabase image, and every existing object's grants made explicit. Client roles lost `TRUNCATE`, `REFERENCES`, `TRIGGER` and `MAINTAIN`, write privileges on the views, and `UPDATE` on sequences. `anon` lost its writes on `Space` and `EXECUTE` on the functions that write. `authenticated` lost `INSERT` on `Space`, since only create-space creates spaces, and `space_insert_policy` was removed.
